  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.3.1: Sprite drawing and a coordinate transform stack. Added Draw.Sprite, which draws a textured sprite immediately with no Scene or Component, configured through SpriteDrawOptions (an explicit texture or a texture path, an optional source rectangle, scale, origin and tint), with implicit conversions from Texture and string and a fluent builder; the engine now ships a small embedded default texture used by sprites with no texture set, and Sprite2D shares the cached texture instead of copying it per instance. Added a coordinate transform stack to Draw (Translate, Scale, Rotate, Push/Pop, and a disposable Draw.Pushed() scope with fluent calls) applied through RenderStates only, so it affects Draw's own output and never the window view, scenes or components, with a per-frame reset that bounds a forgotten Pop to a single frame. Added Draw.DrawMode(Anchor), which sets how the box primitives (Rectangle, Text, Sprite) anchor their position. Moved the drawing option types into the Core.Drawing.DrawOption namespace. Fixes: replaced the oversized 4096x4096 default texture with a 64x64 one and removed an unnecessary GCHandle pin on the default texture bytes. Added UiCanvas.Find<T>() to look up a root or nested UI element by type.",
